result: 'Wrote docs/error-effects.md — formal spec for Jinn''s checked error-effect
  system. Grounded in actual codebase state (existing ast::Fn.error_types, current_fn_error_types
  inference, ErrReturn, landed trait system from 1-4, and the review''s ?-overloading
  concern).


  Covers: (1) principles; (2) canonical prelude Option of T / Result of T,E with combinator
  method surfaces; (3) err + ! E1|E2 declarations as sugar for Result of R,E; (4)
  new ?> propagation operator (distinct from overloaded ?, desugars to match/!); (5)
  checking rules R1-R6 incl. caller-obligation/--strict-errors; (6) From trait for
  type-directed error conversion (one-step, coherence/orphan rule, union disambiguation);
  (7) SCC least-fixpoint error-set inference algorithm; (8) interaction with defer/generators/actors/value-semantics;
  (9) diagnostics; (10) implementation phasing mapped to subtasks 2-2/2-3/2-4; (11)
  full surface-syntax example.


  Updated dependent subtasks 2-2/2-3/2-4 with spec section references.'
description: Write the formal spec for a real checked error-effect system, defining
  how effects are tracked, declared, and checked at compile time. Done when a reviewed
  design doc exists covering syntax, semantics, and inference rules.
